// Explicit extension seam for Fabric tensor inference intents
//
// DESIGN LIMITATION: Kain currently lacks native high-performance tensor
// inference (e.g., ONNX Runtime, TensorRT). This step bridges the Fabric
// intent to an external inference worker (Python or C++).
//
// HOW THIS WORKS:
// We take the trained model weights and inference inputs (e.g., a frame
// buffer for upscaling, or points for neural caching) from Fabric,
// dispatch them via IPC to the inference engine, and return the
// processed tensor data.

